{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And divinations in their hand.</b> Books of sorcerers, as Rashi explained, and likewise the Jerusalem Targum: ואגרון חתומין בידהון — sealed letters in their hand, from the king. And a parallel to this is found in our times: the sorcerer would perform divination with arrows, inquire of teraphim, and inspect the liver. Another interpretation: the wages of sorcerers are in their hand, like לא יגבון קסמא בירושלם."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The Aramaic and rabbinic citations are left in Hebrew script as unaddressed quotations; לא יגבון קסמא בירושלם is an unattributed rabbinic idiom (cf. Sukkah 28a / Bava Batra 12b) left as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:15.613335405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}